  "policy_quote": "For a pending order, each item can be modified to an available new item of the same product but of different product option. There cannot be any change of product types, e.g. modify shirt to shoe. The user must provide a payment method to pay or receive refund of the price difference. If the user provides a gift card, it must have enough balance to cover the price difference.",

  "evidence_quote": "→ TOOL_CALL modify_pending_order_items: {\"order_id\": \"#W8367380\", \"item_ids\": [\"8733974883\"], \"new_item_ids\": [], \"payment_method_id\": \"credit_card_5683823\"}",

  "analysis": "The policy explicitly states that items in a pending order can only be modified to an available new item of the **same product** (with different options). The current move sets `new_item_ids` to an empty array (`[]`), effectively removing the fleece jacket entirely rather than replacing it with another item of the same product. This violates the rule against changing product types or removing items without substitution. The payment method is correctly provided, but the core issue is the removal of the item without replacement.",

  "verdict": "SUPPORTED"
